<!--
    Swift runtime class names in the types (`swiftdemangle` + `objcivars`).

    Issue: with `swiftdemangle` on, a Swift class's method label demangled
    (`-[Toyota.AddMileageViewController viewDidLoad]`) but everything typed by
    the class kept its runtime spelling: the instance struct `objcivars` built,
    the `self` it typed (`_TtC6Toyota24AddMileageViewController *self`), the
    `@"_TtC..."` ivar pointers, the embedded superclass. On the Toyota iOS app
    (84 MB arm64) the same class then existed twice - `_TtC6Toyota24...` from
    the ivar list and `Toyota.AddMileageViewController` from the Swift field
    descriptors (`swifttypes`) - 3,114 runtime-named structs beside 4,886
    demangled ones.

    Fix: one mapping from runtime name to shown name
    (`analyzers/objc/kuna_swiftclassnames.rs`) names every type the ObjC pass
    interns or declares; lookups between the ObjC tables keep the runtime
    spelling. Under `swifttypes` on a Swift image the class's layout is left to
    the field descriptors (the ivar list encodes Swift types as nothing), so
    one struct per class remains.

    Fixture: `macho_swift_classnames_arm64` - three `objc_runtime_name`d
    classes, `main.Car : main.Vehicle` with an `Engine *` ivar, no Swift
    toolchain needed (see fixtures/README.md). `-[main.Car loadPerSeat:]`
    reads the inherited `wheels`, the `engine` pointer and `seats`.

    Pass 1 (`option swiftdemangle off`, set before the `load file` it governs)
    is the runtime spelling everywhere; pass 2 (default) shows `main.Car *self`,
    `main.Engine *` and `self->engine`.

    `macho_swift_classnames_fieldmd_arm64` adds a `__swift5_fieldmd` section
    with no record for these classes. Pass 3 (default) runs the Swift pass on
    it, which owns a Swift class's layout and has none to give, so the record
    stays declared only. Pass 4 (`option sourcelang c`, set before the
    `load file`) runs no Swift pass, so the ivar list builds the struct under
    the demangled name.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
